  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Keeping a 6-card hand with 5 Mountains and 2 spells (Furious Rise and Heartfire) that both require creatures to function. This hand does literally nothing until creatures are drawn off the top, as Furious Rise needs a 4-power creature and Heartfire needs a sacrifice. The hand has zero board presence and no path to affecting the game without topdecking.",
      "action_taken": "Kept a 6-card hand of 5 Mountains, Furious Rise, and Heartfire.",
      "better_line": "Mulligan to 5 hoping for at least one creature. While going to 5 is painful, this 6-card hand is essentially a 0-spell hand since both spells are dead without creatures. A 5-card hand with even one creature would be significantly more functional.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
      "player": "GPT54 Coach",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Opponent's only creature (Crypt Lurker 3/4) has summoning sickness and cannot block. Opponent has zero untapped lands, so no combat tricks are possible. Spiteful Prankster would deal 3 uncontested damage, representing a significant portion of the opponent's life total.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to attack with Spiteful Prankster, dealing 0 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Spiteful Prankster for 3 free damage. There are no possible blockers and no mana available for any interaction.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 84,
      "player": "GPT54 Coach",
      "decision_index": 44,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed with 1 mana available and no other use for it, declining to equip Malefic Scythe (1 soul counter, giving +1/+1) to Bone Picker. This would have made Bone Picker a 4/3 flying deathtouch at no meaningful cost, ready to attack next turn as a stronger threat.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without equipping Malefic Scythe to Bone Picker.",
      "better_line": "Activate Malefic Scythe's equip ability targeting Bone Picker, making it a 4/3 flying deathtouch for next turn's attack.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 117,
      "player": "Gem3P Fate",
      "decision_index": 64,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Cast Burst Lightning while Bone Picker (3/2 flying deathtouch) was on the stack, using their only untapped mana. This prevents them from using Burst Lightning to kill Bone Picker after it resolves (it has 2 toughness, exactly matching Burst Lightning's damage). A 3/2 flying deathtouch creature is a serious threat that Burst Lightning cleanly answers.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Burst Lightning in response to Bone Picker on the stack (likely targeting opponent's face for 2 damage)",
      "better_line": "Let Bone Picker resolve, then cast Burst Lightning targeting Bone Picker to kill it. Removing a 3/2 flying deathtouch creature is far more valuable than 2 damage to the opponent's face.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 116,
      "player": "GPT54 Coach",
      "decision_index": 63,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed in postcombat main with 4 untapped Mountains and Furious Rise in hand castable for {2}{R}. While Furious Rise wouldn't trigger this end step (no 4+ power creature), deploying it now costs nothing meaningful and positions for future card advantage the moment a qualifying creature hits the board (e.g., Pitchburn Devils with any buff, or a future draw). Holding it gains nothing since there's no better use for the mana this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, wasting 4 mana and ending the turn without casting anything.",
      "better_line": "Cast Furious Rise for {2}{R} to have it on board ready to generate card advantage as soon as a 4+ power creature is deployed.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 131,
      "player": "GPT54 Coach",
      "decision_index": 74,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to cast Temur Battle Rage on Spiteful Prankster during combat when the opponent has no blockers and is completely tapped out. This wastes 3 free damage (6 instead of 3). The mana saved doesn't enable anything meaningful - Furious Rise can't trigger without a power 4+ creature, and Pitchburn Devils costs 5 mana. Temur Battle Rage is a combat trick that may not find a better window.",
